        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12438047/comment/12766042",
          "id": "12766042",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=alexander.klimetschek",
            "name": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "key": "alexander.klimetschek",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=alexander.klimetschek&avatarId=25443"
            },
            "displayName": "Alexander Klimetschek",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/Los_Angeles"
          },
          "body": "Ok, I thought it would be enabled by default. Hence I revert my -1 vote.\n\nI would note that one should see this attribute like a password, that then must be set on both the client code and the repository configuration.\n\n> It should rather be easy to write a special login module that can be set by configuration and handles SSO things and co.\n\nAs Felix pointed out to me, certain login mechanisms like openID, which involve multiple http requests, cannot be easily done by a jackrabbit loginmodule.",
          "updateAuthor": {
